<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13572" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĕ-ūro</span></b> , ussi, ustum,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a.,
				to burn up, consume</i> (freq. in the historians; elsewh. rare;
			not in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.:
			pluteos turrium, *<i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 7, 25</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vicum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					10, 4</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agros vicosque (with depopulari),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 39,
					2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">partem Circi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					6, 45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montem Caelium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 64</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frumenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 40, 41</span></i>
			 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of cold, <i>to
			destroy</i> (cf.: aduro, amburo, and Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καίειν</span>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hiems arbores deusserat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					40, 45</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Curt. 8, 9, 12</span></i>. And of destruction by a
			serpent's breath, <i><span class="en">Sen. Clem. 1, 25, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
